<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kara Koyunlu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kara Koyunlu, or Black Sheep Turkomans, were a Turkoman tribal confederation that ruled parts of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the fourteenth and fifteenth centuries. They were rivals of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a>. They absorbed western Persian territories as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a> fragmented.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kara-koyunlu.jpg" alt="Kara Koyunlu" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Demis Map Server · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Timurid_and_Qara_Qoyunlu_domains,_1458.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
